   "category": "correctness",
   "title": "`task_statuses` skips every task after a build that returned composition errors.",
   "body": "The summary is pushed inside the `for task in check_workflow.tasks` loop. The existing `CompositionCheckTask` arm still `break`s as soon as `composition_errors` is non-empty. So when a subgraph check fails composition with errors, `task_summaries` only holds the tasks Studio listed up to and including the build. Operations, lint, proposals, filter, custom and downstream tasks that come after it never appear in `data.task_statuses`. That contradicts the PR and changeset, which say the field \"lists every task in the check\". A script that reads it also can't see that those tasks were BLOCKED, and it gets a different set of tasks depending on the order Studio returns them in.\n\nFix: build `task_summaries` from all tasks before the loop that can break, e.g. `let task_summaries: Vec<_> = check_workflow.tasks.iter().map(|task| CheckTaskSummary { .. }).collect();`. Or replace the `break` with a flag so only the per-task response handling is skipped."
  }
 ],
